      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before the 1964 Olympics, an expressway was built over Nihonbashi, obscuring the classic view of Mount Fuji.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nihonbashi served as the starting point for five Edo‑period routes, linking all of ancient Japan.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic fish market on Nihonbashi became the predecessor of today’s Tsukiji and Toyosu markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nihonbashi"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mitsukoshi, Japan’s first department store, opened in 1904 on Nihonbashi, originally a 1673 kimono shop.",
